{
  "_doc": [
    "Contract corpus for the Go, Rust (and later Swift) session decoders and writers.",
    "Every field object lists all 27 Session fields in Go struct order, defaults included.",
    "Times are [year, month, day, hour, minute, second, nanosecond, utc_offset_seconds].",
    "start_time, queued_at, end_time and exit_code: null means unset; the writer omits the key.",
    "sessions: testdata/sessions/<name> decodes to fields; writing fields gives testdata/written/<name>.",
    "written: extra writer cases; writing fields gives testdata/written/<name>, which decodes back to fields.",
    "via_new_queued: the writer builds the record with NewQueued(cli, mode, model, effort, work_dir, prompt,",
    "  review_scope, group_id), keeps its prompt_preview and prompt_hash, and takes every other field from fields.",
    "  fields.prompt_preview has one U+FFFD for each stray byte of a rune split at byte 100.",
    "  Decoding the record and writing it again gives testdata/written/<stem>.resaved.json."
  ],
